Subject: Omit the clang::annotate refactoring attribute under Fil-C
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
Applies-After: ports/patch/abseil-cpp-20260107.1.patch

ABSL_REFACTOR_INLINE expands to [[clang::annotate("inline-me")]], used by
ABSL_DEPRECATE_AND_INLINE and the deprecated MutexLock(Mutex*) constructors.
Any translation unit that ODR-uses such a function (protobuf's arena.cc,
re2's dfa.cc, ...) gets an `llvm.global.annotations` global with appending
linkage, and FilPizlonator aborts in lockDownLinkage(). The annotation only
feeds Google's internal go/cpp-inliner tool, so it is dropped for Fil-C.
See docs/filc-findings.md; checked by tests/protobuf.nix (protobuf and re2
consumers compile against the installed headers).

diff --git a/absl/base/macros.h b/absl/base/macros.h
index 446a445..844ced8 100644
--- a/absl/base/macros.h
+++ b/absl/base/macros.h
@@ -203,7 +203,11 @@ ABSL_NAMESPACE_END
 // Note: go/cpp-inliner is Google-internal service for automated refactoring.
 // While open-source users do not have access to this service, the macro is
 // provided for compatibility.
-#if ABSL_HAVE_CPP_ATTRIBUTE(clang::annotate)
+// Fil-C: clang::annotate on a function emits an `llvm.global.annotations`
+// global with appending linkage, which the FilPizlonator pass rejects
+// (assertion in lockDownLinkage). The annotation only feeds an external
+// refactoring tool, so drop it.
+#if ABSL_HAVE_CPP_ATTRIBUTE(clang::annotate) && !defined(__FILC__)
 #define ABSL_REFACTOR_INLINE [[clang::annotate("inline-me")]]
 #else
 #define ABSL_REFACTOR_INLINE
